  <item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - Gaza: girl dies after gunfire wounds as camp fire displaces families</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-27/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-27/</guid>
    <description>Limited-source update based on three WAFA reports. Normal provider collection was blocked before fetching, so this is not a complete daily briefing. This edition is text-only. | 3 sources</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - WAFA reports Palestinian killed and several injured in Gaza attacks</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-26/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-26/</guid>
    <description>WAFA reported on October 25 that a Palestinian was killed and several others were injured in an Israeli bombardment of the Sheikh Nasser neighborhood east of Khan Younis. The report also described additional injuries in Jabalia refugee camp and near al-Maghazi refugee camp. | 1 source | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
  <title>Dispatches From Gaza</title>
  <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/</link>
  <description>Daily briefing</description>
  
  
  
  
  
  <item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - &#x27;Gaza&#x27;s suffering has become campaign fodder&#x27;: Palestinians fear the worst from Israel election</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-25/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-25/</guid>
    <description>Humanitarian catastrophe largely ignored as rivals Gadi Eisenkot and Benjamin Netanyahu vow to end Hamas rule As. Israel prepares to go to the polls , Palestinians in Gaza are bracing for an outcome that could shape their future, knowing their fate rests with the country that has reduced much of the territory to rubble and killed nearly 75,000 people. Gaza, where nearly a million displaced Palestinians face dire sanitary conditions, water shortages and the constant threat of Israeli strikes, has been largely absent from the election campaign . | 2 sources | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
<item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - Two Palestinians killed and others injured in strike in Al-Nasr, western Gaza City</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-24/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-24/</guid>
    <description>WAFA reported two Palestinians killed and others injured in an October 23 strike in Al-Nasr, western Gaza City. | 1 source | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - WFP reports October cuts to Gaza food assistance</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-19/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-19/</guid>
    <description>WFP says October 2026 assistance covers 1.1 million people, down from 1.6 million in September 2026, with rations halved and fewer hot meals. The United Nations World Food Programme said on October 19, 2026 that funding shortages have forced it to reduce food assistance in Gaza by around one-third. WFP says it is supporting 1.1 million people in October 2026, down from 1.6 million in September 2026, and that food rations are half the previous allocation. The agency says daily hot meals have been reduced from 250,000 to 150,000 and that about 500,000 people have lost access to critical assistance. This preview reports WFP&#x27;s announcement; it does not infer a different start date or claim the figures are independently measured. | 1 source | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
<item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - Woman reportedly killed east of Khan Younis</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-18/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-18/</guid>
    <description>WAFA, citing medical sources, reports that on October 18 Wijdan Kamal Shurrab, 28, was killed by Israeli gunfire on al-Sikka Street east of Khan Younis. | 3 sources | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
<item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - At least one Palestinian killed in al-Mawasi strike in Rafah; several injured, WAFA reports</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-17/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-17/</guid>
    <description>WAFA reports at least one Palestinian killed and several injured in an Israeli drone strike on al-Mawasi in Rafah, citing a medical source in Gaza. No exact event time is asserted. | 3 sources | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
<item>
    <title>Dispatches From Gaza - UNICEF briefing reports child casualties during the preceding two weeks in Gaza</title>
    <link>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-16/</link>
    <guid>https://dispatches.thebluefernco.com/gaza/editions/2026-10-16/</guid>
    <description>UNICEF Global Deputy Spokesperson Ricardo Pires said at a 16 October Geneva briefing that, in the last two weeks in Gaza, five boys and two girls had been reported killed and at least 33 children seriously injured in air strikes, drone strikes and gunfire; two additional boys died from earlier injuries. This is a reported two-week window, not a count of deaths on 16 October. | 1 source | Limited-source update</description>
  </item>
